   "id": "tla-plus",
   "relation": "family"
  }
 ],
 "level_notes": {
  "1": "Classical B is defined by Abrial's The B-Book (1996) and in practice by ClearSy's B Language Reference Manual for Atelier B (free PDF, linked by section via #page=N). Event-B is defined by Abrial's Modeling in Event-B (2010) and the Rodin/Event-B wiki documents.",
  "0": "Atelier B (ClearSy) is the industrial toolset for classical B; Rodin (Eclipse-based, Java) for Event-B; ProB (Prolog/Java, Düsseldorf) is an animator and model checker for both, whose SableCC grammars are in hhu-stups/probparsers."
 },
